{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/658957-slenderman-for-a-horror","id":658957,"title":"Slenderman for a horror?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-09T22:45:28-07:00","id":658957,"title":"Slenderman for a horror?","content":"In Beast the horrors are often described as, well, beasts. There's dragons, kraken, giant birds of prey and the like, but what about a more modern take on it? Like the title suggests, I'm talking about stuff like Slenderman, but where would you draw the line? Would you let someone's horror be Golden Freddy from FNAF? A Dalek from Doctor Who? A radioactive specter born from dropping the atomic bombs that ended WWII? <br /> <br /> What would you say you're favorite &quot;modern&quot; horror is? <br /> <br /> Personally, I've always liked the idea of <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spring_Heeled_Jack\" target=\"_blank\">Spring Heeled Jack</a> 'cuz I' my weird like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5257-queshire","name":"Queshire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T04:12:53-07:00","id":659225,"title":"","content":"The first draft mentioned &quot;plague zombies&quot; as a possible Soul/Horror - and those are only about forty-fifty years old. <b>Night of the Living Dead</b> really created the concept . . . so you <i>can</i> do more contemporary (or human-like) Beasts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i><u>Edit:</u> </i>I've always liked Slenderman as a modern day incarnation of Nyarlathotep. Wrong game line, though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T05:38:36-07:00","id":659258,"title":"","content":"In general, I'd say go for it. Notably, I'd focus on pitching the idea less on familiarity and more on nature. Why is a Five Nights at Freddie's character scary? Why is a Dalek scary? Focus on those when building your character.<br /> <br /> As for the second question, what is &quot;modern&quot;? Because if you mean within the last century, then the Alien Invader. Just a classic that helped to shape the genre in a lot of ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T07:27:09-07:00","id":659359,"title":"","content":"You know how in the game where you have to collect the 8 pages while Slendy stalks you, one of the pages says &quot;always watches, no eyes&quot;? And how Slendy is apparently capable of being anywhere without you noticing he's watching you? That may suggest Ugallu, but a big part of what makes him scary is how little we know about him and how he could be right behind you. Besides, it isn't like people are scared of Slendy because he knows how to expose your secrets or what have you. I'd say he is an Eshmaki. Several theories exist that try to explain why he kidnaps people, often children. One of them says he is a faerie who punishes bad children by scaring them half to death, and only allows them to go back home if they admit what they did. That would suggest Hunger For Punishment. However, I find it more likely that his habit of stalking, tormenting, kidnapping and supposedly killing people is caused by Hunger For Prey. He might have Kinship with True Fae, allowing him to develop Nightmares for locating and stalking people more effectively, in an Ugallu-like way. His Lair is probably <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/416820-if-the-slender-man-was-a-true-fae-what-would-his-realm-be-like?p=416928#post416928\"><b>something like this.</b></a> I already have some stats for him written up, I'll add the Beast traits later and post them in this thread.<br /> <br /> I like to think that, if Slender Man is not a Beast's Soul/Horror, he is a True Fae or a very mysterious Unchained Demon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 09-10-2015, 05:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T08:50:33-07:00","id":659412,"title":"","content":"Why I like my flying jellyfish: nothing fancy, just pure, existential dread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T01:51:06-07:00","id":660516,"title":"","content":"When doing presentation about <b>Beast</b> game for mine RPG club, I added more modern takes on Horrors to every Family, beside mythical monsters. So here is mine short list:<ul><li><b>Anakim</b> - <i>Godzilla</i> - Giant atomic created lizard you cannot run from and can stomp all your life with one blow.</li> <li><b>Eshmaki</b> - <i>Slenderman</i> and <i>Monster Under a Bad</i> - Things you know that ARE THERE, SOMEWHERE &lt;Ominous Music&gt;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> <li><b>Makara</b> - <i>Cthulhu</i> - You cannot go better with alien tentacle horror from the depths of ocean. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> <li><b>Namtaru</b> - <i>Freddy Kruger</i> - The demonic &quot;ghost&quot; of serial killer, so foul, his face is causing disgust in everyone.</li> <li><b>Ugallu</b> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/625727-beast-ugallu-everything-knowing-webpage-horror\"><i>Internet Horror</i></a> - Web spidery thing that knows EVERYTHING about you, and can use it all the time your dirtiest secrets.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T08:38:59-07:00","id":687095,"title":"","content":"Here we go. Any feedback is appreciated. I went with the powers and abilities he shows more often, since his list has become quite a grab bag over the course of the Mythos. I also tried to make him powerful but not invincible. Whatever Social Merits and Professional Training he might have as a result of his human side is best left to ST fiat, I believe.<br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Eshmaki<br /> <b>Hunger: </b>Prey/Punishment<br /> <br /> <b>Legend: </b>Watchful/Unexpected<br /> <b>Life: </b>Parental<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 4, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 6, Dexterity 4, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 6, Manipulation 3, Composure 6<br /> <br /> <b>Horror Attributes:</b> Power 12, Finesse 10, Resistance 8, Size 7<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics 2, Computer 1, Crafts 2, Investigation (Searching) 4, Medicine 2, Occult 4, Politics 1, Science 2<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics (Chasing) 3, Brawl (Claws &amp; Tentacles) 3, Drive 1, Firearms 1, Larceny 3, Stealth (Plain Sight) 6, Survival (Forests &amp; Woodlands) 4, Weaponry 1<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken 2, Empathy (Children) 3, Expression 2, Intimidation (Appearing Out Of Nowhere) 5, Persuasion 3, Streetwise 1, Subterfuge 3<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area Of Expertise (Searching), Patient, Tolerance For Biology, Direction Sense (Advanced), Ambidextrous, Double Jointed (Advanced), Demolisher 3, Choke Hold, Hardy 3, Iron Stamina 3, Fleet Of Foot 3, Parkour 3, Iron Will, Indomitable, Fame 2 (Advanced 2), Retainer X (Proxies), Fist Of Nightmares, Hunger Management 3, Guilty Pleasure (Children), <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/653956-beasts-with-multiple-hungers?p=658370#post658370\"><b>Broad Palate</b></a><br /> <br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 4 + Athletics/Brawl/Weaponry<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 10<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 16<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <br /> <b>Lair:</b> 8<br /> <br /> <b>Lair Traits:</b> Fog, Maze, Poor Light, Undergrowth, Disruption, Mirages<br /> <br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> Alien Allure, Eye Of Heaven, From The Shadows, Limb From Limb, Looming Presence, Mimir\u2019s Wisdom, Monster Of The Deep, Needs Must, Relentless Hunter, Shadowed Soul, Siren\u2019s Treacherous Song, Unbreakable<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> All Your Teeth Are Falling Out, Fear Is Contagious, Run Away, You Are Not Alone, You Can\u2019t Wake Up, You Will Never Rest, Tabula Rasa, You Are Lost","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 10-03-2015, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T15:34:45-08:00","id":1017357,"title":"","content":"Slenderman is blatantly a Giant. Everybody knows he's supposed to be super tall and lanky.<br /> <br /> Second, he fits with the theme of powerlessness, because even if you play his game and pass his trials, you still lose!<br /> <br /> <br /> You can't fight him (you die if you so much as stare at him), and you can't escape him because he can teleport at will. The only thing you can do is wait for the inevitable. Maybe the authorities will find your corpse impaled on a tree branch later... if you're lucky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T17:50:44-08:00","id":1017406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/658957-slenderman-for-a-horror?p=1017357#post1017357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slenderman is blatantly a Giant. Everybody knows he's supposed to be super tall and lanky.<br /> <br /> Second, he fits with the theme of powerlessness, because even if you play his game and pass his trials, you still lose!<br /> <br /> <br /> You can't fight him (you die if you so much as stare at him), and you can't escape him because he can teleport at will. The only thing you can do is wait for the inevitable. Maybe the authorities will find your corpse impaled on a tree branch later... if you're lucky.</div> </div> </div> </div> That makes sense, but I don't think he would make much use of the Anakim Birthright. The theme you described can also be phrased as Fear Of Exposure, and Slendy would find the Ugallu Birthright much more useful, methinks.<br /> <br /> Also, I decided to rewrite my character sheet for him, with optional Beast-Shapes if you want him to be an Incarnate.<br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Ugallu<br /> <b>Hunger: </b>Prey<br /> <b>Myth:</b> The Unfathomable, Ever-Watching Boogeyman<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 6, Resolve 5<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 6, Dexterity 5, Stamina 5<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 7, Manipulation 4, Composure 5<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics 3, Computer 1, Crafts 2, Investigation (Searching) 4, Medicine 2, Occult 4, Politics 0, Science 2<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics (Chasing) 4, Brawl (Claws And Tentacles) 4, Drive 0, Firearms 0, Larceny 3, Stealth (Plain Sight) 6, Survival (Forests And Woodlands) 4, Weaponry 0<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken 2, Empathy (Children) 3, Expression 2, Intimidation (Appearing Out Of Nowhere) 5, Persuasion 4, Streetwise 0, Subterfuge 3<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Area Of Expertise (Searching, Plain Sight), Demolisher 2, Direction Sense (Epic), Double-Jointed (Advanced), Eidetic Memory (Advanced), Fame 3 (Advanced 3: Shaken), Hunger Management 3, Indomitable (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration\"><b>Advanced</b></a>), Iron Will, Patient (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration\"><b>Advanced 3</b></a>), Retainer (Proxies), Striking Looks 2 (Nightmarish)<br /> <br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 9<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 10<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 64<br /> <b>Health:</b> 18<br /> <b>Lair:</b> 8<br /> <br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> Alien Allure, From The Shadows, Limb From Limb, Looming Presence, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=833241#post833241\"><b>In My Image</b></a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=876121#post876121\"><b>Inescapable</b></a>, Monster Of The Deep, Needs Must, Relentless Hunter, Shadowed Soul, Siren\u2019s Treacherous Song, Unbreakable<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> Fear Is Contagious, Run Away, You Are Not Alone, You Can\u2019t Wake Up, You Will Never Rest, Tabula Rasa, You Are Lost<br /> <br /> <b>Horror Traits: </b>Power 12, Finesse 12, Resistance 10, Size 13, Health 18, Defense 10, Initiative 12, Speed 17<br /> <br /> <b>Lair Traits:</b> Fog, Maze, Poor Light, Undergrowth, Disruption, Mirages<br /> <br /> <b>Beast-Shapes: </b>Legendary Size, Multiple Appendages x 2 (Arms), One With The Shadows, Terrible Mien, Superior Atavism (From The Shadows, Shadowed Soul, Inescapable)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-14-2016, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}